      "widgets_values": [
        "I use this for putting style back onto things, including peoples faces back onto grey 3D face models made in previous workflows. It's bodgy, but worked for my restyling needs at the time (April 2025).\n\n\nput reference image here for the look of the face\n\nand describe what you need in the green prompt text area.\n\nexample: \"30 year old man looking at the camera. realistic. colour. 4K, high quality.\"\n\nset image size in \"Empty LAtent Image\"\n\nset denoise strength in the Ksampler will guide how it adhers to the images and controlnet depthmap. You dont get much improvement over 25 steps and 8 is good for starting with.\n\nthis will provide style from reference image and positional structure from controlnets. \n\nthe image will also be passed through reactor to get it back to same look as reference image and saved out."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
